CLIF 1.0
namespace: clarion
clan: probe-ambiguity
source-language: en-US
target-language: zh-CN
title: "Minimal-pair diagnostic set where the brief is decisive"
info: "The probe stratum measures what a translation brief is worth: entries come in minimal pairs whose source text is identical or nearly so, and only one CLIF field (emotion, type, context or max-width) tells the two members apart. A translation that ignores that field must fail at least one member. Every item is original text written for CLARION, drawn from generic software, transit, stage, warehouse and support scenarios."
standard: "Use one space between Han text and Latin letters or digits, and fullwidth punctuation inside Han sentences. Render the emotion tag in the wording, particles and punctuation, never as a neutral gloss. Honor the type field's register: a label stays a bare noun, a sentence is a full instruction, an idiom is an idiomatic wish, a proper noun is a place name. Choose the referent the context line names. Fit the declared max-width in display cells, where Latin letters and digits count one cell and Han or fullwidth characters count two. No textbook jargon."

[emotion.reading]
context: "Spoken lines that come in pairs; the emotion tag, not the words, decides how the line should sound."
type: dialogue

<probe-01a>
source: "Oh, that's just wonderful."
target: "真是太好了。"
status: final
emotion: [joyful, grateful]
context: "The speaker has just opened an acceptance letter and means the compliment warmly."

<probe-01b>
source: "Oh, that's just wonderful."
target: "哦，这下可真是「好」得很。"
status: final
emotion: [angry, playful]
context: "The speaker has just watched the plan fall apart; the line is bitter irony."

<probe-02a>
source: "After you."
target: "您先请，别客气。"
status: final
emotion: [polite, calm]
context: "A cafe customer holds the door open and genuinely lets the other person go first."

<probe-02b>
source: "After you."
target: "您先请——别磨蹭。"
status: final
emotion: [polite, angry]
context: "The speaker gestures toward the unlit stairwell; the courtesy is really an order to go first."

<probe-03a>
source: "Well, here we go again."
target: "好嘞，咱们再来一次！"
status: final
emotion: [joyful, playful]
context: "Two friends line up for another round of the board game; said with a grin."

<probe-03b>
source: "Well, here we go again."
target: "唉，怎么又来了。"
status: final
emotion: [sad, calm]
context: "A repair worker returns to the same machine for the third time; said with a sigh."

<probe-04a>
source: "Just relax."
target: "放松，一切都会好的。"
status: final
emotion: [calm, hopeful]
context: "A nurse reassures a patient before a routine procedure."

<probe-04b>
source: "Just relax."
target: "放松点，别乱动。"
status: final
emotion: [serious, angry]
context: "A guard tells a cornered intruder to stop moving; the tone is steady, not warm."

[type.register]
context: "Pairs where the same English string changes rendering with its type; honor the register the type implies."

